('/anybike-global.html#global-story-honda-super-cub-the-small-motorcycle-with-a-global-story','Honda Super Cub: the small motorcycle with a global story','Honda’s step-through Super Cub debuted in 1958. Its approachable controls made it a practical choice for everything from commuting to deliveries.','anybike-global.html','<article class="tile" data-manufacturer="Honda" data-type="scooters,roadsters"><div class="tag">Japan · Motorcycle history</div><h3>Honda Super Cub: the small motorcycle with a global story</h3><p>Honda’s step-through Super Cub debuted in 1958. Its approachable controls made it a practical choice for everything from commuting to deliveries.</p><p><a href="https://global.honda/en/newsroom/news/2017/c171019aeng.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Honda''s production history ↗</a></p><p><a href="/motorcycle-brand.html?make=Honda">Browse Honda motorcycle models →</a></p></article>','published','fb1e6babb874ddf79c55e5173a31332b698e23ef7b4c10e98df9bbb31f0e3f7a'),
('/anybike-global.html#global-story-vespa-how-practical-transport-became-a-design-icon','Vespa: how practical transport became a design icon','The original Vespa met Italy’s need for affordable transport in 1946. Its leg shield and step-through bodywork remain part of its identity.','anybike-global.html','<article class="tile" data-manufacturer="Vespa" data-type="scooters,classics"><div class="tag">Italy · Industrial design</div><h3>Vespa: how practical transport became a design icon</h3><p>The original Vespa met Italy’s need for affordable transport in 1946. Its leg shield and step-through bodywork remain part of its identity.</p><p><a href="https://www.piaggiogroup.com/en/group/history" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Piaggio company history ↗</a></p><p><a href="/motorcycle-brand.html?make=Vespa">See Vespa models →</a></p></article>','published','e0ed425f2fe3a51f2867a15983f092d0d47598aa28fdc67572dc17d81578c0e3'),
('/global/burt-munro-worlds-fastest-indian.html','Burt Munro and the World''s Fastest Indian','How a New Zealander spent decades developing a 1920 Indian Scout and set a land-speed record at Bonneville in 1967.','anybike-global.html','<article class="lead-story" data-country="New Zealand, United States" data-manufacturer="Indian Motorcycle" data-topics="Racing, Heritage, Rider stories" id="global-story-burt-munro-and-the-world-s-fastest-indian">
    <figure>
      <img src="/assets/global/burt-munro-indian-scout-special.webp" alt="Red streamlined bodywork of Burt Munro’s 1920 Indian Scout Special on display" width="1440" height="892" fetchpriority="high">
      <figcaption>Munro’s Indian Scout Special · Photo courtesy of <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Munro_Indian_Scout_Special_1920,_01.jpg">Kgbo</a> · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a> · Resized</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="lead-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow">New Zealand · Land-speed racing</div>
      <h2 id="lead-title"><a href="/global/burt-munro-worlds-fastest-indian.html">Burt Munro and the World''s Fastest Indian</a></h2>
      <p>How a New Zealander spent decades developing a 1920 Indian Scout and set a land-speed record at Bonneville in 1967.</p>
      <div class="link-actions"><a class="button" href="/global/burt-munro-worlds-fastest-indian.html">Read Burt Munro’s story →</a><a href="/indian-motorcycles.html">Indian Motorcycle history and models →</a></div>
      <div class="lead-more"><a href="/anybike-global.html?country=New%20Zealand#story-finder">More from New Zealand</a> · <a href="/anybike-global.html?topic=Racing#story-finder">More racing stories</a></div>
    </div>
  </article>','published','4f373a45cadbf972181e35ef68691669fbfe9e201573c685d02f14f54d11a23a'),
('/global/yamaha-niken-leaning-three-wheel-design.html','Yamaha NIKEN and the two-front-wheel idea','Why Yamaha developed a leaning three-wheeler, and how its front-end engineering changes the way we think about motorcycle design.','anybike-global.html','<article class="tile" data-manufacturer="Yamaha" data-type="touring"><figure class="featured-photo">
  <img src="/assets/global/yamaha-niken-paris.webp" width="850" height="566" alt="Yamaha NIKEN cutaway with its twin front wheels at the Paris Motor Show" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
  <figcaption>Yamaha NIKEN cutaway · Photo courtesy of <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yamaha_Niken_-_Mondial_de_l%27Automobile_de_Paris_2018_-_001.jpg">Thesupermat</a> · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a> · Resized and cropped</figcaption>
</figure><div class="tag">Japan · Design</div><h3><a href="/global/yamaha-niken-leaning-three-wheel-design.html">Yamaha NIKEN and the two-front-wheel idea</a></h3><p>Why Yamaha developed a leaning three-wheeler, and how its front-end engineering changes the way we think about motorcycle design.</p>
<p class="related-link"><a href="/models/yamaha/niken.html">Yamaha NIKEN model guide →</a></p></article>','published','56b447e97c4c9f08fe2ecf824529cff62b5814ce10a8a701578ab85c6d98dfce'),
('/global/can-am-pulse-origin-electric-motorcycles.html','Can-Am Pulse and Origin: city or dual-sport?','Two different approaches to electric motorcycling, and why charging, conditions and riding purpose matter.','anybike-global.html','<article class="tile" data-manufacturer="Can-Am" data-type="roadsters,off-road"><figure class="featured-photo">
